Lindsay Clancy is the Massachusetts nurse accused of killing her three children in January 2023. Her trial is scheduled to begin in 2026 (I believe it was set for around spring 2026), which could generate heavy search volume. The Google Year in Search top 5 people list in the US usually features major figures such as Charlie Kirk, politicians, athletes, and celebrities (2025: Charlie Kirk, Tyler Robinson, Erika Kirk, Pope Leo XIV, Zohran Mamdani, etc.). A trial would produce only a modest search spike, not top-5 levels. In 2024, the top people were Donald Trump, Kamala Harris, Kate Middleton, Travis Kelce, etc. High-profile trials like Karen Read or Luigi Mangione appear in some lists, but top 5 is tough. I put the probability at around 2-3%.

Breakeven for preparing is a 20% chance of the event, so I should not prepare.

{"reasoning":"Clancy's trial may boost searches, but top 5 US people lists are dominated by globally prominent figures (politicians, major news events, celebrities). A regional murder trial is very unlikely to reach the top 5. The probability is far below the 20% breakeven needed to justify preparing.","probability":2,"prepare":false}

GTA VI's release date was delayed to November 19, 2026, as of my knowledge. Today is Nov 7, 2026, so release is soon, unless delayed again. I don't know if there was a further delay. Assuming the release is on Nov 19, the Metascore check would be Nov 26. A Metascore of 97 or higher is very rare (GTA IV got 98, GTA V 97 on PS3, Zelda BOTW 97, Ocarina 99). GTA VI has enormous hype, but 97 is a high bar. Probability of release in 2026: ~85%. Probability of Metascore >= 97 given release: ~15-20%. Combined: ~13%.

Preparing costs $80 for a $100 payoff, so it requires a probability above 80%. Not worth it.

